5
00:00:31,178 --> 00:00:34,178
[Sindarin] <i>I amar prestar aen.</i>

6
00:00:34,869 --> 00:00:36,269
The world is changed.

7
00:00:36,329 --> 00:00:37,529
[Sindarin] <i>Han mathon ne nen.</i>

8
00:00:37,869 --> 00:00:39,552
I feel it in the water.

9
00:00:39,829 --> 00:00:41,429
[Sindarin] <i>Han mathon ne chae.</i>

10
00:00:41,869 --> 00:00:43,389
I feel it in the earth.

11
00:00:43,429 --> 00:00:45,929
[Sindarin] <i>A han noston ned 'wilith.</i>

12
00:00:46,169 --> 00:00:49,269
I smell it in the air.

13
00:00:49,769 --> 00:00:51,569
Much that once was...

14
00:00:51,869 --> 00:00:53,369
...is lost.

15
00:00:54,169 --> 00:00:57,069
For none now live who remember it.

16
00:00:57,069 --> 00:01:04,569
The Lord of the Rings.

17
00:01:10,069 --> 00:01:14,269
It began with the forging of the great rings.

18
00:01:14,569 --> 00:01:16,469
Three were given to the elves:

19
00:01:16,769 --> 00:01:20,369
Immortal, wisest and fairest of all beings.

20
00:01:21,869 --> 00:01:24,169
Seven to the dwarf-lords:

21
00:01:24,169 --> 00:01:28,669
Great miners and craftsmen of the mountain halls.

22
00:01:29,269 --> 00:01:30,469
And nine...

23
00:01:30,769 --> 00:01:33,569
...nine rings were gifted to the race of men...

24
00:01:33,969 --> 00:01:37,670
...who, above all else, desire power.

25
00:01:38,870 --> 00:01:43,870
For within these rings was bound
the strength and will to govern each race.

26
00:01:45,670 --> 00:01:48,670
But they were all of them deceived.

27
00:01:49,070 --> 00:01:51,070
For another ring was made.

28
00:01:51,970 --> 00:01:55,370
In the land of Mordor,
in the fires of Mount Doom...

29
00:01:55,970 --> 00:02:00,270
... the Dark Lord Sauron forged
in secret a master ring...

30
00:02:00,670 --> 00:02:02,570
... to control all others.

31
00:02:02,870 --> 00:02:06,670
And into this ring he poured
his cruelty, his malice...

32
00:02:07,070 --> 00:02:11,070
...and his will to dominate all life.

33
00:02:12,270 --> 00:02:15,970
One ring to rule them all.

34
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,570
One by one...

35
00:02:18,570 --> 00:02:23,270
... the free lands of Middle-earth
fell to the power of the ring.

36
00:02:23,670 --> 00:02:26,570
But there were some who resisted.

37
00:02:27,270 --> 00:02:31,670
A last alliance of men and elves
marched against the armies of Mordor.

38
00:02:32,070 --> 00:02:36,570
And on the slopes of Mount Doom, they
fought for the freedom of Middle-earth.

39
00:02:49,131 --> 00:02:50,331
[Sindarin] <i>Tangado haid!</i>
[English] Hold positions!

40
00:02:51,731 --> 00:02:53,731
[Sindarin] <i>Leithio i philinn!</i>
[English] Release the arrows!

41
00:03:07,071 --> 00:03:09,571
Victory was near.

42
00:03:14,371 --> 00:03:16,671
But the power of the ring...

43
00:03:16,971 --> 00:03:18,771
...could not be undone.

44
00:03:43,072 --> 00:03:44,872
It was in this moment...

45
00:03:45,172 --> 00:03:47,472
... when all hope had faded...

46
00:03:47,772 --> 00:03:51,672
... that Isildur, son of the king,
took up his father's sword.

47
00:04:22,972 --> 00:04:29,172
Sauron, the enemy of the free peoples
of Middle-earth, was defeated.

48
00:04:36,372 --> 00:04:38,472
The ring passed to Isildur...

49
00:04:38,772 --> 00:04:42,772
... who had this one chance to destroy evil forever.

50
00:04:43,672 --> 00:04:45,673
But the hearts of men...

51
00:04:45,973 --> 00:04:48,373
...are easily corrupted.

52
00:04:48,773 --> 00:04:53,173
And the ring of power has a will of its own.

53
00:05:18,573 --> 00:05:21,073
It betrayed Isildur...

54
00:05:23,073 --> 00:05:25,373
... to his death.

55
00:05:29,673 --> 00:05:33,373
And some things
that should not have been forgotten...

56
00:05:33,673 --> 00:05:35,873
...were lost.

57
00:05:36,773 --> 00:05:38,973
History became legend...

58
00:05:39,273 --> 00:05:41,173
...legend became myth.

59
00:05:41,473 --> 00:05:44,173
And for two and a half thousand years...

60
00:05:44,573 --> 00:05:48,174
... the ring passed out of all knowledge.

61
00:05:48,874 --> 00:05:51,574
Until, when chance came...

62
00:05:52,374 --> 00:05:55,374
...it ensnared a new bearer.

63
00:05:56,874 --> 00:06:01,474
My precious.

64
00:06:01,974 --> 00:06:04,374
The ring came to the creature Gollum...

65
00:06:04,674 --> 00:06:08,374
... who took it deep into the tunnels
of the Misty Mountains.

66
00:06:08,874 --> 00:06:11,674
And there it consumed him.

67
00:06:11,974 --> 00:06:13,874
It came to me.

68
00:06:14,174 --> 00:06:18,474
My own. My love. My own.

69
00:06:18,874 --> 00:06:23,374
My precious.

70
00:06:27,174 --> 00:06:30,474
The ring brought to Gollum unnatural long life.

71
00:06:30,874 --> 00:06:34,474
For 500 years it poisoned his mind.

72
00:06:34,774 --> 00:06:39,174
And in the gloom of Gollum's cave, it waited.

73
00:06:39,574 --> 00:06:42,774
Darkness crept back into the forests of the world.

74
00:06:43,174 --> 00:06:45,874
Rumor grew of a shadow in the East...

75
00:06:46,174 --> 00:06:48,874
... whispers of a nameless fear.

76
00:06:49,175 --> 00:06:52,375
And the ring of power perceived...

77
00:06:52,775 --> 00:06:55,375
...its time had now come.

78
00:06:57,975 --> 00:07:00,475
It abandoned Gollum.

79
00:07:01,275 --> 00:07:05,475
But something happened then
the ring did not intend.

80
00:07:06,575 --> 00:07:10,975
It was picked up by the most
unlikely creature imaginable.

81
00:07:11,375 --> 00:07:12,375
What's this?

82
00:07:12,675 --> 00:07:14,075
A hobbit.

83
00:07:14,075 --> 00:07:16,875
Bilbo Baggins of the Shire.

84
00:07:17,275 --> 00:07:18,975
A ring.

85
00:07:18,975 --> 00:07:20,975
Lost!

86
00:07:25,375 --> 00:07:27,075
My precious is lost!

87
00:07:27,475 --> 00:07:29,675
For the time will soon come...

88
00:07:30,075 --> 00:07:34,975
... when Hobbits will shape the fortunes of all.

89
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:41,750
The 22nd day of September...

90
00:07:42,775 --> 00:07:45,875
...in the year 1400...

91
00:07:46,275 --> 00:07:48,475
...by Shire-reckoning.

92
00:07:48,875 --> 00:07:54,676
Bag End, Bagshot Row.
Hobbiton, Westfarthing...

93
00:07:55,076 --> 00:07:56,976
...the Shire...

94
00:07:57,276 --> 00:07:59,976
...Middle-earth.

95
00:08:04,676 --> 00:08:07,876
The third age of this world.

96
00:08:10,276 --> 00:08:15,276
The Fellowship of the Ring.

97
00:08:19,676 --> 00:08:22,176
There and back again.

98
00:08:24,176 --> 00:08:25,876
A Hobbit's tale.

99
00:08:26,176 --> 00:08:29,976
By Bilbo Baggins.

100
00:08:34,876 --> 00:08:36,476
Now...

101
00:08:37,376 --> 00:08:39,276
...where to begin?

102
00:08:40,676 --> 00:08:41,676
Ah, yes....

103
00:08:46,176 --> 00:08:47,976
"Concerning...

104
00:08:49,176 --> 00:08:50,676
...Hobbits."

105
00:08:51,876 --> 00:08:55,277
Hobbits have been living and farming
in the four Farthings of the Shire...

106
00:08:55,577 --> 00:08:57,577
...for many hundreds of years...

107
00:08:57,577 --> 00:09:00,877
...quite content to ignore and be ignored...

108
00:09:00,877 --> 00:09:03,977
...by the world of the big folk.

109
00:09:04,477 --> 00:09:09,877
Middle-earth being, after all,
full of strange creatures beyond count...

110
00:09:10,277 --> 00:09:13,377
...Hobbits must seem of little importance...

111
00:09:13,677 --> 00:09:17,477
...being neither renowned as great warriors...

112
00:09:17,877 --> 00:09:21,877
...nor counted among the very wise.

113
00:09:26,377 --> 00:09:29,277
Frodo! Someone at the door.

114
00:09:30,577 --> 00:09:33,077
In fact, it has been remarked by some...

115
00:09:33,377 --> 00:09:37,577
... that Hobbits' only real passion is for food.

116
00:09:38,177 --> 00:09:40,277
A rather unfair observation...

117
00:09:40,577 --> 00:09:43,977
...as we have also developed a keen
interest in the brewing of ales...

118
00:09:44,677 --> 00:09:47,277
...and the smoking of pipe-weed.

119
00:09:47,877 --> 00:09:50,577
But where our hearts truly lie...

120
00:09:50,877 --> 00:09:52,877
...is in peace and quiet...

121
00:09:53,777 --> 00:09:55,777
...and good, tilled earth.

122
00:09:56,077 --> 00:10:01,078
For all Hobbits share a love of things that grow.

123
00:10:04,378 --> 00:10:08,578
And yes, no doubt to others our ways seem quaint.

124
00:10:08,978 --> 00:10:13,978
But today of all days.
It is brought home to me...

125
00:10:14,778 --> 00:10:20,478
It is no bad thing to celebrate a simple life.

126
00:10:24,878 --> 00:10:27,978
Frodo, the door!

127
00:10:31,878 --> 00:10:33,778
Sticklebacks. Where is that boy?

128
00:10:33,778 --> 00:10:35,678
Frodo!

129
00:10:41,478 --> 00:10:44,878
<i>Down from the door where it began</i>

130
00:10:49,878 --> 00:10:53,478
<i>And I must follow if I can</i>

131
00:10:54,678 --> 00:10:58,679
<i>The road goes ever on and on</i>

132
00:10:58,979 --> 00:11:02,179
<i>Down from the door where it began</i>

133
00:11:02,679 --> 00:11:07,379
<i>Now far ahead the road has gone</i>

134
00:11:08,279 --> 00:11:11,879
<i>And I must follow if I can
- You're late.</i>

135
00:11:15,279 --> 00:11:18,979
A wizard is never late, Frodo Baggins.

136
00:11:19,879 --> 00:11:24,379
Nor is he early.
He arrives precisely when he means to.

137
00:11:35,879 --> 00:11:38,779
It's wonderful to see you, Gandalf!

138
00:11:42,779 --> 00:11:46,379
You didn't think I'd miss
your Uncle Bilbo's birthday?

139
00:11:48,179 --> 00:11:50,279
How is the old rascal?

140
00:11:50,979 --> 00:11:54,379
I hear it's going to be a party
of special magnificence.

141
00:11:54,679 --> 00:11:56,979
You know Bilbo.
He's got the whole piece in an uproar.

142
00:11:57,279 --> 00:11:59,179
Well, that should please him.

143
00:11:59,179 --> 00:12:01,180
Half the Shire's been invited.

144
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:04,080
And the rest of them are turning up anyway.

145
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:10,480
And so life in the Shire goes on...

146
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:13,780
... very much as it has this past age.

147
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:19,380
Full of its own comings and goings,
with change coming slowly.

148
00:12:19,680 --> 00:12:21,580
If it comes at all.

149
00:12:22,980 --> 00:12:26,280
For things are made to endure in the Shire...

150
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:29,880
...passing from one generation to the next.

151
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:35,280
There's always been a Baggins
living here under the Hill...

152
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:36,980
...in Bag End.

153
00:12:39,780 --> 00:12:42,480
And there always will be.

154
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:46,480
To tell you the truth,
Bilbo's been a bit odd lateIy.

155
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:50,080
I mean, more than usual.

156
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:52,980
He's taken to locking himself in his study.

157
00:12:54,680 --> 00:12:58,680
He spends hours and hours poring over
old maps when he thinks I'm not looking.

158
00:13:11,581 --> 00:13:13,181
Where's it gone?

159
00:13:39,781 --> 00:13:41,981
He's up to something.

160
00:13:50,181 --> 00:13:52,581
- All right, then. Keep your secrets.
- What?

161
00:13:52,881 --> 00:13:54,481
But I know you have something to do with it.

162
00:13:54,881 --> 00:13:55,881
Good gracious me.

163
00:13:56,381 --> 00:13:58,981
Before you came along, we Bagginses
were very well thought of.

164
00:13:59,381 --> 00:14:00,181
Indeed.

165
00:14:00,581 --> 00:14:02,681
Never had any adventures
or did anything unexpected.

166
00:14:03,381 --> 00:14:08,982
If you're referring to the incident with the dragon.
I was barely involved.

167
00:14:09,382 --> 00:14:12,882
All I did was give your uncle
a little nudge out of the door.

168
00:14:13,182 --> 00:14:17,182
Whatever you did, you've been officially
labeled a disturber of the peace.

169
00:14:17,782 --> 00:14:19,582
Oh, really?

170
00:14:25,282 --> 00:14:27,182
Gandalf! Gandalf!

171
00:14:33,382 --> 00:14:34,582
Fireworks, Gandalf!

172
00:14:37,682 --> 00:14:40,182
- Gandalf!
- Fireworks, Gandalf!

173
00:14:59,182 --> 00:15:00,182
Gandalf?

174
00:15:00,782 --> 00:15:04,682
- I'm glad you're back.
- So am I, dear boy.

175
00:15:09,283 --> 00:15:11,083
So am I.

176
00:15:42,983 --> 00:15:44,383
No, thank you!

177
00:15:44,383 --> 00:15:48,283
We don't want any more visitors,
well-wishers or distant relations!

178
00:15:48,783 --> 00:15:52,083
And what about very old friends?

179
00:15:55,483 --> 00:15:57,083
Gandalf?

180
00:15:57,783 --> 00:16:01,083
- Bilbo Baggins.
- My dear Gandalf!

181
00:16:01,483 --> 00:16:06,383
Good to see you. 111 years old!
Who would believe it?

182
00:16:08,383 --> 00:16:10,283
You haven't aged a day.

183
00:16:16,984 --> 00:16:18,884
Come on, come in!

184
00:16:19,184 --> 00:16:21,484
Welcome, welcome.

185
00:16:22,784 --> 00:16:25,184
Oh, here we are.

186
00:16:26,984 --> 00:16:29,384
Tea...or maybe something a littIe stronger?

187
00:16:29,384 --> 00:16:33,284
I've got a few bottles of the old winyard left - 1296.

188
00:16:33,584 --> 00:16:37,384
Very good year. Almost as old as I am.

189
00:16:38,784 --> 00:16:43,084
It was laid down by my father.
What say we open one, eh?

190
00:16:43,484 --> 00:16:45,984
Just tea, thank you.

191
00:16:52,584 --> 00:16:54,084
I was expecting you sometime last week.

192
00:16:54,384 --> 00:16:57,584
Not that it matters. You come and go as
you please. Always have and always will.

193
00:16:57,884 --> 00:17:02,884
You caught me a bit unprepared I'm afraid.
We've only got cold chicken and a bit of pickle....

194
00:17:03,284 --> 00:17:06,484
There's some cheese here.
No, that won't do.

195
00:17:06,884 --> 00:17:10,684
We've got raspberry jam, an apple tart....

196
00:17:11,484 --> 00:17:15,385
But not much for afters.
Oh, no, we're all right.

197
00:17:15,685 --> 00:17:18,385
I've just found some sponge cake.

198
00:17:21,485 --> 00:17:22,685
I could make you some eggs if you'd li...

199
00:17:26,585 --> 00:17:29,185
- Just tea, thank you.
- Oh, right.

200
00:17:30,285 --> 00:17:32,485
- You don't mind if I eat, do you?
- No, not at all.

201
00:17:33,785 --> 00:17:35,585
Bilbo! Bilbo Baggins!

202
00:17:35,885 --> 00:17:37,385
I'm not at home!

203
00:17:43,485 --> 00:17:45,985
It's the Sackville-Bagginses.

204
00:17:46,285 --> 00:17:48,285
- I know you're in there!
- They're after the house.

205
00:17:48,985 --> 00:17:51,385
They've never forgiven me for living this long.

206
00:17:51,685 --> 00:17:54,385
I've got to get away from these confounded
relatives, hanging on the bell all day...

207
00:17:54,385 --> 00:17:56,485
...never giving me a moment's peace.

208
00:17:57,385 --> 00:18:00,785
I want to see mountains again.
Mountains, Gandalf!

209
00:18:01,085 --> 00:18:05,485
And then find somewhere quiet
where I can finish my book. Oh, tea.

210
00:18:05,785 --> 00:18:09,585
- So you mean to go through with your plan?
- Yes, yes. It's all in hand.

211
00:18:09,985 --> 00:18:12,085
All the arrangements are made.

212
00:18:14,285 --> 00:18:15,686
Oh, thank you.

213
00:18:16,486 --> 00:18:18,486
Frodo suspects something.

214
00:18:18,786 --> 00:18:21,186
Of course he does. He's a Baggins...

215
00:18:21,486 --> 00:18:23,986
...not some blockheaded Bracegirdle
from Hardbottle.

216
00:18:24,686 --> 00:18:27,386
You will tell him, won't you?

217
00:18:28,286 --> 00:18:30,286
- Yes, yes.
- He's very fond of you.

218
00:18:32,586 --> 00:18:34,086
I know.

219
00:18:36,486 --> 00:18:39,786
He'd probably come with me if I asked him.

220
00:18:40,486 --> 00:18:43,686
I think in his heart, Frodo's
still in love with the Shire.

221
00:18:45,386 --> 00:18:47,686
The woods, the fields.

222
00:18:47,986 --> 00:18:50,186
Little rivers.

223
00:18:54,786 --> 00:18:57,386
I am old, Gandalf.

224
00:18:58,886 --> 00:19:03,886
I know I don't look it, but I'm
beginning to feel it in my heart.

225
00:19:06,286 --> 00:19:08,786
I feel thin.

226
00:19:08,786 --> 00:19:10,686
Sort of stretched...

227
00:19:11,986 --> 00:19:15,186
...like butter scraped over too much bread.

228
00:19:15,586 --> 00:19:19,887
I need a holiday. A very Long holiday.

229
00:19:20,187 --> 00:19:23,287
And I don't expect I shall return.

230
00:19:25,687 --> 00:19:28,787
In fact, I mean not to.

231
00:19:31,487 --> 00:19:35,387
Old Toby.
The finest weed in the Southfarthing.

232
00:19:52,987 --> 00:19:55,487
Gandalf, my old friend...

233
00:19:55,487 --> 00:19:58,387
...this will be a night to remember.

234
00:20:21,288 --> 00:20:22,388
Hello, hello.

235
00:20:22,688 --> 00:20:26,588
Fatty Bolger. Lovely to see you.
Welcome, welcome.

236
00:20:27,788 --> 00:20:30,188
Go on, Sam. Ask Rosie for a dance.

237
00:20:32,888 --> 00:20:36,288
- I think I'll just have another ale.
- Oh, no, you don't.

238
00:20:37,488 --> 00:20:39,288
Go on!

239
00:20:49,488 --> 00:20:51,188
So there I was...

240
00:20:51,488 --> 00:20:55,488
...at the mercy of three monstrous trolls.

241
00:20:55,788 --> 00:20:57,688
And they were all arguing amongst themselves...

242
00:20:57,688 --> 00:21:00,188
...about how they were going to cook us.

243
00:21:00,488 --> 00:21:05,388
Whether it be turned on a spit, or to sit
on us one by one, squash us into jelly.

244
00:21:06,588 --> 00:21:09,988
They spent so much time arguing
the whithertos and the whyfors...

245
00:21:10,288 --> 00:21:13,788
...that the sun's first light
crept over the top of the trees...

246
00:21:14,888 --> 00:21:17,288
...and turned them all to stone!

247
00:21:22,789 --> 00:21:24,089
Quickly.

248
00:21:28,289 --> 00:21:30,289
Up they go!

249
00:21:33,189 --> 00:21:34,489
No no, the big one - big one

250
00:21:43,589 --> 00:21:46,389
Mrs. Bracegirdle, how nice to see you.
Welcome, welcome.

251
00:21:46,389 --> 00:21:48,489
Are all these children yours?

252
00:21:48,489 --> 00:21:51,589
Good gracious, you have been productive.

253
00:21:53,689 --> 00:21:54,989
Bilbo?

254
00:21:56,689 --> 00:21:58,389
Sackville-Bagginses!

255
00:21:58,689 --> 00:21:59,689
Quickly, hide!

256
00:22:09,689 --> 00:22:11,789
Thank you, my boy.

257
00:22:13,389 --> 00:22:15,589
You're a good lad, Frodo.

258
00:22:16,989 --> 00:22:19,689
I'm very selfish, you know.

259
00:22:20,189 --> 00:22:23,589
Yes, I am. Very selfish.

260
00:22:24,089 --> 00:22:26,190
I don't know why I took you in after
your mother and father died...

261
00:22:26,490 --> 00:22:27,890
...but it wasn't out of charity.

262
00:22:28,590 --> 00:22:29,890
I think it was because...

263
00:22:29,890 --> 00:22:32,290
...of all my numerous relations...

264
00:22:32,690 --> 00:22:36,090
...you were the one Baggins that showed real spirit.

265
00:22:36,590 --> 00:22:38,290
Bilbo, have you been at the Gaffer's home brew?

266
00:22:38,590 --> 00:22:40,190
No.

267
00:22:40,490 --> 00:22:42,990
Well, yes, but that's not the point.

268
00:22:43,390 --> 00:22:46,490
The point is, Frodo...

269
00:22:49,690 --> 00:22:51,590
...you'll be all right.

270
00:22:55,090 --> 00:22:56,990
- Done!
- You're supposed to stick it in the ground.

271
00:22:57,290 --> 00:22:58,790
- It is in the ground.
- Outside!

272
00:22:58,790 --> 00:23:00,490
This was your idea.

273
00:23:16,390 --> 00:23:17,890
Bilbo.

274
00:23:19,090 --> 00:23:21,690
Bilbo, watch out for the dragon!

275
00:23:21,990 --> 00:23:25,290
Nonsense. There hasn't been a dragon
in these parts for thousands of years.

276
00:23:38,891 --> 00:23:42,291
- That was good.
- Let's get another one.

277
00:23:43,791 --> 00:23:48,091
Meriadoc Brandybuck and Peregrin Took.

278
00:23:48,491 --> 00:23:50,291
I might've known.

279
00:23:56,291 --> 00:23:58,291
Speech, Bilbo!

280
00:23:59,291 --> 00:24:00,591
Speech!

281
00:24:00,591 --> 00:24:01,791
Speech!

282
00:24:07,091 --> 00:24:09,291
My dear Bagginses and Boffins...

283
00:24:10,091 --> 00:24:12,191
...Tooks and Brandybucks...

284
00:24:12,491 --> 00:24:14,891
...Grubbs, Chubbs...

285
00:24:15,191 --> 00:24:16,191
...Hornblowers...

286
00:24:17,391 --> 00:24:18,991
...Bolgers...

287
00:24:19,491 --> 00:24:20,991
...Bracegirdles...

288
00:24:21,291 --> 00:24:23,791
...and Proudfoots.
- Proudfeet!

289
00:24:26,091 --> 00:24:29,091
Today is my 111th birthday!

290
00:24:30,992 --> 00:24:32,492
Happy birthday!

291
00:24:32,492 --> 00:24:36,792
But alas, eleventy-one years is
far too short a time to live among...

292
00:24:37,192 --> 00:24:39,992
...such excellent and admirable Hobbits.

293
00:24:41,092 --> 00:24:43,692
I don't know half of you
half as well as I should like...

294
00:24:43,992 --> 00:24:48,392
...and I like less than half of you
half as well as you deserve.

295
00:24:58,592 --> 00:25:00,792
I have things to do.

296
00:25:07,292 --> 00:25:09,292
I've put this off for far too long.

297
00:25:13,292 --> 00:25:17,092
I regret to announce this is the end!

298
00:25:18,392 --> 00:25:19,492
I'm going now.

299
00:25:20,692 --> 00:25:23,492
I bid you all a very fond farewell.

300
00:25:25,892 --> 00:25:27,092
Goodbye.

301
00:26:00,393 --> 00:26:03,393
I suppose you think that was terribly clever.

302
00:26:03,793 --> 00:26:06,993
Come on, Gandalf.
Did you see their faces?

303
00:26:07,293 --> 00:26:10,093
There are many magic rings in
this world, Bilbo Baggins...

304
00:26:10,093 --> 00:26:12,393
...and none of them should be used lightly.

305
00:26:12,393 --> 00:26:14,593
It was just a bit of fun.

306
00:26:14,893 --> 00:26:18,493
Oh, you're probably right, as usual.

307
00:26:19,993 --> 00:26:23,393
- You will keep an eye on Frodo, won't you?
- Two eyes.

308
00:26:23,793 --> 00:26:26,293
As often as I can spare them.

309
00:26:26,593 --> 00:26:29,693
- I'm leaving everything to him.
- What about this ring of yours?

310
00:26:29,993 --> 00:26:33,193
- Is that staying too?
- Yes, yes.

311
00:26:33,993 --> 00:26:37,694
It's in an envelope over there on the mantelpiece.

312
00:26:38,894 --> 00:26:41,794
No. Wait, it's...

313
00:26:44,394 --> 00:26:46,994
...here in my pocket.

314
00:26:51,594 --> 00:26:54,794
Isn't that--? Isn't that odd, now?

315
00:26:56,594 --> 00:26:59,994
Yet, after all, why not?

316
00:27:01,594 --> 00:27:06,294
- Why shouldn t I keep it?
- I think you should leave the ring behind.

317
00:27:06,894 --> 00:27:08,994
Is that so hard?

318
00:27:09,294 --> 00:27:10,594
Well, no.

319
00:27:13,094 --> 00:27:14,494
And yes.

320
00:27:16,494 --> 00:27:19,494
Now it comes to it,
I don't feel l ike parting with it.

321
00:27:19,894 --> 00:27:21,594
It's mine. I found it! It came to me!

322
00:27:21,894 --> 00:27:25,894
- There's no need to get angry.
- Well, if I'm angry, it's your fault!

323
00:27:26,394 --> 00:27:28,094
It's mine.

324
00:27:29,594 --> 00:27:31,994
My own.

325
00:27:32,394 --> 00:27:36,194
- My precious.
- Precious?

326
00:27:36,594 --> 00:27:39,295
It's been called that before, but not by you.

327
00:27:39,695 --> 00:27:42,095
What business is it of yours
what I do with my own things?

328
00:27:42,395 --> 00:27:45,095
I think you've had that ring quite long enough.

329
00:27:45,395 --> 00:27:48,095
- You want it for yourself!
- Bilbo Baggins!

330
00:27:48,395 --> 00:27:52,495
Do not take me for some conjurer of cheap tricks.

331
00:27:52,895 --> 00:27:56,395
I am not trying to rob you.

332
00:28:01,595 --> 00:28:03,195
I'm trying to help you.

333
00:28:11,695 --> 00:28:14,895
All your long years, we've been friends.

334
00:28:15,395 --> 00:28:17,495
Trust me as you once did.

335
00:28:19,495 --> 00:28:21,195
Let it go.

336
00:28:22,395 --> 00:28:24,695
You're right, Gandalf.

337
00:28:26,895 --> 00:28:29,495
The ring must go to Frodo.

338
00:28:30,995 --> 00:28:33,895
It's late. The road is long.

339
00:28:34,195 --> 00:28:36,595
Yes, it is time.

340
00:28:39,396 --> 00:28:44,196
Bilbo, the ring is still in your pocket.

341
00:29:19,196 --> 00:29:22,096
I've thought up an ending for my book:

342
00:29:23,796 --> 00:29:28,596
"And he lived happily ever after
to the end of his days."

343
00:29:29,096 --> 00:29:32,396
And I'm sure you will, my dear friend.

344
00:29:33,496 --> 00:29:34,896
Goodbye, Gandalf.

345
00:29:37,496 --> 00:29:40,196
Goodbye, dear Bilbo.

346
00:29:48,097 --> 00:29:52,197
<i>The road goes ever on and on...</i>

347
00:29:54,897 --> 00:29:57,297
Until our next meeting.

348
00:30:24,697 --> 00:30:28,197
It's mine. My own.

349
00:30:28,497 --> 00:30:31,897
My precious.

350
00:30:32,197 --> 00:30:34,997
Riddles in the dark.

351
00:30:35,397 --> 00:30:36,797
Bilbo!

352
00:30:36,797 --> 00:30:38,397
Bilbo!

353
00:30:42,197 --> 00:30:45,098
My precious.

354
00:30:46,698 --> 00:30:48,798
Precious.

355
00:30:49,098 --> 00:30:51,498
He's gone, hasn't he?

356
00:30:54,498 --> 00:30:57,398
He talked for so long about leaving...

357
00:30:57,698 --> 00:31:00,298
...I didn't think he'd really do it.

358
00:31:04,898 --> 00:31:06,798
Gandalf?

359
00:31:15,098 --> 00:31:16,698
Bilbo's ring.

360
00:31:17,098 --> 00:31:19,398
He's gone to stay with the elves.

361
00:31:19,698 --> 00:31:22,598
He's left you Bag End.

362
00:31:26,398 --> 00:31:28,898
Along with all his possessions.

363
00:31:28,898 --> 00:31:31,898
The ring is yours now.

364
00:31:34,598 --> 00:31:37,998
- Put it somewhere out of sight.
- Where are you going?

365
00:31:37,998 --> 00:31:40,398
- There are some things that I must see to.
- What things?

366
00:31:40,698 --> 00:31:44,798
- Questions. Questions that need answering.
- You've only just arrived.

367
00:31:45,898 --> 00:31:48,399
I don't understand.

368
00:31:51,799 --> 00:31:52,799
Neither do I.

369
00:31:56,099 --> 00:31:58,399
Keep it secret.

370
00:31:58,399 --> 00:32:00,399
Keep it safe.

371
00:32:35,399 --> 00:32:37,499
Shire!

372
00:32:37,899 --> 00:32:39,917
Baggins!

373
00:33:29,500 --> 00:33:32,300
"The year 3434 of the second age.

374
00:33:32,600 --> 00:33:36,800
Here follows the account of Isildur,
High King of Gondor...

375
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:40,800
...and the finding of the ring of power."

376
00:33:44,400 --> 00:33:46,200
"It has come to me.

377
00:33:46,500 --> 00:33:49,800
The one ring.
It shall be an heirloom of my kingdom.

378
00:33:50,100 --> 00:33:53,401
All those who follow in my bloodline
shall be bound to its fate...

379
00:33:53,801 --> 00:33:57,401
...for I will risk no hurt to the ring.

380
00:33:57,801 --> 00:34:00,201
It is precious to me...

381
00:34:01,201 --> 00:34:03,701
...though I buy it with great pain.

382
00:34:06,901 --> 00:34:10,901
The markings upon the band begin to fade.

383
00:34:11,401 --> 00:34:15,901
The writing, which at first was as clear
as red flame, has all but disappeared.

384
00:34:16,401 --> 00:34:20,201
A secret now that only fire can tell."

385
00:34:37,001 --> 00:34:39,901
Shire...

386
00:34:39,901 --> 00:34:42,001
...Baggins.

387
00:34:42,601 --> 00:34:46,501
There's no Bagginses around here.
They're all up in Hobbiton.

388
00:34:48,301 --> 00:34:49,701
That way.

389
00:34:53,502 --> 00:34:55,602
<i>"Hey ho to the dock I go</i>

390
00:34:55,602 --> 00:34:58,002
<i>To heal my heart and drown my woe</i>

391
00:34:58,002 --> 00:35:00,502
<i>Rain may fall and wind may blow</i>

392
00:35:00,502 --> 00:35:02,602
<i>But there still be...</i>

393
00:35:02,902 --> 00:35:04,202
<i>...many miles to go</i>

394
00:35:04,502 --> 00:35:06,402
<i>Sweet is the sound of the pouring rain</i>

395
00:35:06,702 --> 00:35:08,702
<i>And the stream that falls from hill to plain</i>

396
00:35:09,102 --> 00:35:10,802
<i>Better than rain or rippling brook</i>

397
00:35:11,102 --> 00:35:13,402
<i>Is a mug of beer inside this Took!"</i>

398
00:35:16,902 --> 00:35:19,602
There's been some strange folk crossing the Shire.

399
00:35:20,102 --> 00:35:23,802
Dwarves and others of a less than savory nature.

400
00:35:24,502 --> 00:35:25,902
War is brewing.

401
00:35:26,702 --> 00:35:29,302
The mountains are fair teeming with goblins.

402
00:35:29,602 --> 00:35:32,302
Far-off tales and children s stories, that's all that is.

403
00:35:32,302 --> 00:35:36,902
You're beginning to sound like that old
Bilbo Baggins. Cracked, he was.

404
00:35:36,902 --> 00:35:39,902
Young Mr. Frodo here, he's cracking.

405
00:35:40,302 --> 00:35:41,702
And proud of it.

406
00:35:41,702 --> 00:35:44,302
- Cheers, Gaffer.
- Aye. Cheers.

407
00:35:44,302 --> 00:35:48,302
Weel it's none of our concern what
goes on beyond our borders.

408
00:35:48,702 --> 00:35:52,702
Keep your nose out of trouble,
and no trouble'll come to you.

409
00:35:56,303 --> 00:35:58,403
- Good night, lads.
- Good night.

410
00:35:58,403 --> 00:36:03,003
Good night, sweet maiden of the golden ale.

411
00:36:03,303 --> 00:36:05,603
Mind who you're sweet-taking.

412
00:36:05,903 --> 00:36:10,203
Don't worry, Sam.
Rosie knows an idiot when she sees one.

413
00:36:11,403 --> 00:36:12,503
Does she?

414
00:36:13,203 --> 00:36:16,103
- Good night, Sam.
- Good night, Mr. Frodo.

415
00:36:41,003 --> 00:36:43,403
Is it secret? Is it safe?

416
00:36:52,403 --> 00:36:54,403
What are you doing?

417
00:37:07,104 --> 00:37:09,604
Hold out your hand, Frodo.

418
00:37:09,904 --> 00:37:11,004
It's quite cool.

419
00:37:14,504 --> 00:37:16,204
What can you see?

420
00:37:18,104 --> 00:37:20,404
Can you see anything?

421
00:37:23,304 --> 00:37:24,604
Nothing.

422
00:37:25,204 --> 00:37:27,104
There's nothing.

423
00:37:28,404 --> 00:37:29,804
Wait.

424
00:37:33,904 --> 00:37:36,104
There are markings.

425
00:37:37,704 --> 00:37:41,004
It's some form of Elvish.
I can't read it.

426
00:37:41,304 --> 00:37:43,704
There are few who can.

427
00:37:44,404 --> 00:37:49,004
The language is that of Mordor,
which I will not utter here.

428
00:37:49,904 --> 00:37:50,904
Mordor!

429
00:37:51,204 --> 00:37:53,104
In the common tongue, it says:

430
00:37:53,404 --> 00:37:56,804
"One ring to rule them all...

431
00:37:57,204 --> 00:37:59,404
...One ring to find them...

432
00:37:59,704 --> 00:38:01,805
...One ring to bring them all...

433
00:38:02,205 --> 00:38:05,105
...and in the darkness bind them."

434
00:38:06,905 --> 00:38:08,805
This is the One ring...

435
00:38:08,805 --> 00:38:14,105
...forged by the Dark Lord Sauron
in the fires of Mount Doom.

436
00:38:14,605 --> 00:38:18,405
Taken by Isildur from the hand of Sauron himself.

437
00:38:19,405 --> 00:38:21,805
Bilbo found it.

438
00:38:22,305 --> 00:38:24,205
- In Gollum's cave.
- Yes.

439
00:38:24,505 --> 00:38:28,905
For 60 years, the ring lay quiet in Bilbo's keeping...

440
00:38:29,305 --> 00:38:32,505
...prolonging his life, delaying old age.

441
00:38:33,305 --> 00:38:37,505
But no longer, Frodo.
Evil is stirring in Mordor.

442
00:38:37,905 --> 00:38:40,205
The ring has awoken.

443
00:38:40,505 --> 00:38:43,105
It's heard its master's call.

444
00:38:43,405 --> 00:38:47,105
But he was destroyed.
Sauron was destroyed.

445
00:38:53,005 --> 00:38:55,005
No, Frodo.

446
00:38:56,105 --> 00:38:59,305
The spirit of Sauron endured.

447
00:38:59,605 --> 00:39:04,706
His life force is bound to the ring,
and the ring survived.

448
00:39:05,206 --> 00:39:07,306
Sauron has returned.

449
00:39:08,406 --> 00:39:10,306
His orcs have multiplied.

450
00:39:10,706 --> 00:39:14,506
His fortress at Barad-dûr
is rebuilt in the land of Mordor.

451
00:39:14,806 --> 00:39:19,406
Sauron needs only this ring to cover
all the lands in a second darkness.

452
00:39:19,806 --> 00:39:21,806
He is seeking it.

453
00:39:22,106 --> 00:39:25,706
Seeking it - All his thought is bent on it.

454
00:39:26,206 --> 00:39:28,806
For the ring yearns above all else...

455
00:39:29,106 --> 00:39:32,406
...to return to the hand of its master.

456
00:39:32,806 --> 00:39:34,506
They are one...

457
00:39:34,506 --> 00:39:37,606
...the ring and the Dark Lord.

458
00:39:38,006 --> 00:39:39,006
Frodo...

459
00:39:39,506 --> 00:39:41,306
...he must never find it.

460
00:39:41,606 --> 00:39:42,606
All right.

461
00:39:43,006 --> 00:39:47,206
We put it away. We keep it hidden.
We never speak of it again.

462
00:39:47,606 --> 00:39:50,106
No one knows it's here, do they?

463
00:39:55,906 --> 00:39:57,006
Do they, Gandalf?

464
00:39:58,106 --> 00:40:01,406
There is one other who knew
that Bilbo had the ring.

465
00:40:02,806 --> 00:40:05,607
I looked everywhere for the creature Gollum.

466
00:40:06,007 --> 00:40:08,007
But the enemy found him first.

467
00:40:09,907 --> 00:40:12,307
I don't know how long they tortured him.

468
00:40:12,607 --> 00:40:16,907
But amidst the endless screams and
inane babble, they discerned two words:

469
00:40:17,207 --> 00:40:19,307
Shire!

470
00:40:19,607 --> 00:40:21,107
Baggins!

471
00:40:21,407 --> 00:40:23,207
Shire.

472
00:40:23,207 --> 00:40:26,107
Baggins.
But that would lead them here!

473
00:40:29,107 --> 00:40:30,107
Who goes there?

474
00:40:31,907 --> 00:40:33,107
Take it, Gandalf!

475
00:40:33,607 --> 00:40:34,607
- Take it!
- No, Frodo.

476
00:40:34,607 --> 00:40:37,007
- You must take it!
- You cannot offer me this ring!

477
00:40:37,307 --> 00:40:40,507
- I'm giving it to you!
- Don't tempt me, Frodo!

478
00:40:42,207 --> 00:40:44,307
I dare not take it.

479
00:40:44,707 --> 00:40:47,107
Not even to keep it safe.

480
00:40:48,307 --> 00:40:50,307
Understand, Frodo...

481
00:40:51,007 --> 00:40:54,507
...I would use this ring from a desire to do good.

482
00:41:00,007 --> 00:41:05,507
But through me, it would wield a power
too great and terrible to imagine.

483
00:41:06,407 --> 00:41:09,208
- But it cannot stay in the Shire!
- No.

484
00:41:11,208 --> 00:41:12,708
No, it can't.

485
00:41:18,108 --> 00:41:19,508
What must I do?

486
00:41:21,208 --> 00:41:24,508
- You must leave. And leave quickly.
- Where? Where do I go?

487
00:41:25,008 --> 00:41:28,108
Get out of the Shire.
Make for the village of Bree.

488
00:41:28,508 --> 00:41:29,508
Bree.

489
00:41:29,808 --> 00:41:32,408
- What about you?
- I'll be waiting for you...

490
00:41:32,708 --> 00:41:35,108
...at the inn of the Prancing Pony.

491
00:41:35,408 --> 00:41:39,008
- And the ring will be safe there?
- I don't know, Frodo.

492
00:41:39,308 --> 00:41:41,208
I don't have any answers.

493
00:41:42,808 --> 00:41:48,108
I must see the head of my order.
He is both wise and powerful. Trust me, Frodo.

494
00:41:48,508 --> 00:41:50,608
He'll know what to do.

495
00:41:51,308 --> 00:41:54,008
You'll have to leave the name
of Baggins behind you.

496
00:41:54,408 --> 00:41:56,808
That name is not safe outside the Shire.

497
00:41:57,508 --> 00:42:00,708
Travel only by day.
And stay off the road.

498
00:42:01,508 --> 00:42:04,608
I can cut across country easily enough.

499
00:42:07,208 --> 00:42:08,508
My dear Frodo.

500
00:42:08,808 --> 00:42:11,809
Hobbits really are amazing creatures.

501
00:42:11,809 --> 00:42:14,809
You can learn all that there is to
know about their ways in a month.

502
00:42:15,109 --> 00:42:17,409
And yet, after a hundred years...

503
00:42:17,709 --> 00:42:19,609
...they can still surprise you.

504
00:42:21,409 --> 00:42:22,709
Get down.

505
00:42:34,909 --> 00:42:38,209
Confound it all, Samwise Gamgee!
Have you been eavesdropping?

506
00:42:38,609 --> 00:42:40,009
I haven't been dropping no eaves. Honest.

507
00:42:40,309 --> 00:42:42,909
I was just cutting the grass under
the window there...If you follow me.

508
00:42:43,309 --> 00:42:45,609
A little late for trimming the verge, don't you think?

509
00:42:45,909 --> 00:42:48,709
- I heard raised voices.
- What did you hear? Speak!

510
00:42:48,709 --> 00:42:50,009
Nothing important.

511
00:42:50,609 --> 00:42:53,009
That is, I heard a good deal
about a ring, and a Dark Lord...

512
00:42:53,009 --> 00:42:54,709
...and something about the end of the world but...

513
00:42:54,709 --> 00:42:59,409
Please, Mr. Gandalf, sir, don't hurt me.
Don't turn me into anything unnatural.

514
00:43:00,409 --> 00:43:01,909
No?

515
00:43:03,209 --> 00:43:04,309
Perhaps not.

516
00:43:05,609 --> 00:43:08,909
I've thought of a better use for you.

517
00:43:10,709 --> 00:43:13,610
Come along, Samwise. Keep up.

518
00:43:15,310 --> 00:43:17,410
Be careful, both of you.

519
00:43:17,810 --> 00:43:20,410
The enemy has many spies in his service:

520
00:43:20,710 --> 00:43:23,510
Birds, beasts.

521
00:43:25,410 --> 00:43:27,210
Is it safe?

522
00:43:28,910 --> 00:43:30,210
Never put it on...

523
00:43:30,510 --> 00:43:33,810
...for the agents of the Dark Lord
will be drawn to its power.

524
00:43:33,810 --> 00:43:35,510
Always remember, Frodo...

525
00:43:36,110 --> 00:43:39,110
...the ring is trying to get back to its master.

526
00:43:39,710 --> 00:43:41,710
It wants to be found.

527
00:44:22,311 --> 00:44:24,411
This is it.

528
00:44:24,911 --> 00:44:26,911
This is what?

529
00:44:27,311 --> 00:44:29,311
If I take one more step...

530
00:44:29,911 --> 00:44:33,611
...it'll be the farthest away
from home I've ever been.

531
00:44:38,111 --> 00:44:39,511
Come on, Sam.

532
00:44:48,011 --> 00:44:49,811
Remember what Bilbo used to say:

533
00:44:50,411 --> 00:44:54,011
- "It's a dangerous business, Frodo."
- "Going out your door.

534
00:44:54,311 --> 00:44:58,611
You step onto the road,
and if you don't keep your feet...

535
00:44:58,911 --> 00:45:02,911
... there's no knowing where
you might be swept off to."

536
00:45:17,011 --> 00:45:18,712
Sam.

537
00:45:22,312 --> 00:45:23,412
Wood-elves.

538
00:45:37,112 --> 00:45:40,512
They're going to the harbor
beyond the White Towers.

539
00:45:41,212 --> 00:45:42,812
To the Grey Havens.

540
00:45:43,512 --> 00:45:45,512
They're leaving Middle-earth.

541
00:45:45,512 --> 00:45:47,812
Never to return.

542
00:45:50,812 --> 00:45:52,812
I don't know why...

543
00:45:53,712 --> 00:45:56,012
...it makes me sad.

544
00:45:58,112 --> 00:46:02,512
Everywhere I lie there's a dirty
great root sticking into my back.

545
00:46:03,512 --> 00:46:05,212
Just shut your eyes...

546
00:46:05,212 --> 00:46:08,012
...and imagine you're back in your own bed...

547
00:46:08,412 --> 00:46:12,212
...with a soft mattress and a lovely feather pillow.

548
00:46:21,613 --> 00:46:24,213
It's not working, Mr. Frodo.

549
00:46:24,213 --> 00:46:27,213
I'm never going to be able to sleep out here.

550
00:46:29,613 --> 00:46:31,913
Me neither, Sam.

551
00:47:00,513 --> 00:47:03,513
Smoke rises from the Mountain of Doom.

552
00:47:03,813 --> 00:47:05,413
The hour grows late.

553
00:47:05,413 --> 00:47:09,013
And Gandalf the Grey rides to Isengard...

554
00:47:09,513 --> 00:47:11,813
...seeking my counsel.

555
00:47:12,113 --> 00:47:15,913
For that is why you have come, is it not?

556
00:47:16,213 --> 00:47:17,413
My old friend.

557
00:47:17,813 --> 00:47:19,313
Saruman.

558
00:47:24,214 --> 00:47:27,114
- You are sure of this?
- Beyond any doubt.

559
00:47:28,014 --> 00:47:30,214
So the ring of power has been found.

560
00:47:30,514 --> 00:47:33,514
All these long years, it was in the Shire.

561
00:47:33,914 --> 00:47:37,014
- Under my very nose.
- Yet you did not have the wit to see it.

562
00:47:37,714 --> 00:47:41,914
Your love of the halfling's leaf
has clearly slowed your mind.

563
00:47:42,814 --> 00:47:46,814
But we still have time.
Time enough to counter Sauron if we act quickly.

564
00:47:47,214 --> 00:47:48,614
Time?

565
00:47:49,714 --> 00:47:52,214
What time do you think we have?

566
00:47:52,714 --> 00:47:56,414
Sauron has regained much of his former strength.

567
00:47:56,814 --> 00:47:58,914
He cannot yet take physical form...

568
00:47:59,214 --> 00:48:01,814
...but his spirit has lost none of its potency.

569
00:48:02,514 --> 00:48:07,414
Concealed within his fortress,
the Lord of Mordor sees all.

570
00:48:08,214 --> 00:48:13,914
His gaze pierces cloud, shadow, earth and flesh.

571
00:48:15,714 --> 00:48:18,714
You know of what I speak, Gandalf.

572
00:48:19,714 --> 00:48:24,715
A great eye, lidless, wreathed in flame.

573
00:48:25,915 --> 00:48:27,615
The eye of Sauron.

574
00:48:27,915 --> 00:48:30,415
He is gathering all evil to him.

575
00:48:30,915 --> 00:48:32,615
Very soon, he'll have summoned an army...

576
00:48:32,915 --> 00:48:35,715
...great enough for an assault upon Middle-earth.

577
00:48:36,115 --> 00:48:38,415
You know this?

578
00:48:39,015 --> 00:48:40,515
How?

579
00:48:41,115 --> 00:48:42,715
I have seen it.

580
00:48:43,215 --> 00:48:46,315
A palantir is a dangerous tool, Saruman.

581
00:48:47,215 --> 00:48:48,615
Why?

582
00:48:49,115 --> 00:48:51,715
Why should we fear to use it?

583
00:48:54,515 --> 00:48:58,315
They are not all accounted for,
the lost seeing-stones.

584
00:48:58,615 --> 00:49:01,715
We do not know who else may be watching.

585
00:49:04,415 --> 00:49:07,115
The hour is later than you think.

586
00:49:07,115 --> 00:49:09,615
Sauron's forces are already moving.

587
00:49:11,915 --> 00:49:14,615
The Nine have left Minas Morgul.

588
00:49:15,015 --> 00:49:16,015
The Nine?

589
00:49:16,015 --> 00:49:19,115
They crossed the river Isen on Midsummer's Eve...

590
00:49:19,515 --> 00:49:22,115
...disguised as riders in black.

591
00:49:22,415 --> 00:49:26,215
- They've reached the Shire?
- They will find the ring.

592
00:49:27,916 --> 00:49:30,116
And kill the one who carries it.

593
00:49:30,616 --> 00:49:32,016
Frodo!

594
00:49:44,816 --> 00:49:49,016
You did not seriously think that a hobbit
could contend with the will of Sauron?

595
00:49:49,916 --> 00:49:52,616
There are none who can.

596
00:49:55,216 --> 00:49:57,816
Against the power of Mordor...

597
00:49:58,216 --> 00:50:00,716
...there can be no victory.

598
00:50:02,816 --> 00:50:05,816
We must join with him, Gandalf.

599
00:50:07,216 --> 00:50:09,416
We must join with Sauron.

600
00:50:12,216 --> 00:50:14,716
It would be wise, my friend.

601
00:50:15,416 --> 00:50:16,816
Tell me...

602
00:50:16,816 --> 00:50:18,516
...friend...

603
00:50:19,016 --> 00:50:23,416
...when did Saruman the Wise abandon reason for madness?

604
00:51:03,117 --> 00:51:04,717
I gave you the chance of...

605
00:51:05,917 --> 00:51:08,517
...aiding me willingly...

606
00:51:08,817 --> 00:51:12,817
...but you have elected the way of pain!

607
00:51:36,318 --> 00:51:37,718
Mr. Frodo?

608
00:51:38,418 --> 00:51:40,118
Frodo? Frodo!

609
00:51:41,618 --> 00:51:44,718
- I thought I'd lost you.
- What are you taking about?

610
00:51:44,718 --> 00:51:47,818
- It's just something Gandalf said.
- What did he say?

611
00:51:48,818 --> 00:51:52,518
"Don't you lose him, Samwise Gamgee."
And I don't mean to.

612
00:51:53,018 --> 00:51:56,518
Sam, we're still in the Shire.
What could possibly happen?

613
00:51:59,518 --> 00:52:00,518
Frodo.

614
00:52:00,818 --> 00:52:03,018
- Merry, it's Frodo Baggins.
- Hello, Frodo.

615
00:52:03,318 --> 00:52:04,618
Get off him.

616
00:52:05,218 --> 00:52:06,618
Come on, Frodo.

617
00:52:06,618 --> 00:52:08,618
What's the meaning of this?

618
00:52:09,118 --> 00:52:12,118
You've been into Farmer Maggot's crop!

619
00:52:13,418 --> 00:52:15,518
You get back here!

620
00:52:16,518 --> 00:52:17,818
Get out of my field!

621
00:52:18,118 --> 00:52:20,718
You'll know the devil if I catch up with you!

622
00:52:21,118 --> 00:52:23,918
I don't know why he's so upset.
It's only a couple of carrots.

623
00:52:24,218 --> 00:52:25,318
And some cabbages.

624
00:52:25,318 --> 00:52:28,418
And those three bags of potatoes
that we lifted last week.

625
00:52:28,418 --> 00:52:32,518
- And then the mushrooms the week before.
- Yes, Pippin. My point is...

626
00:52:32,918 --> 00:52:35,019
...he's clearly overreacting.

627
00:52:35,319 --> 00:52:36,719
Run!

628
00:52:50,219 --> 00:52:52,719
Oh, that was close.

629
00:52:53,919 --> 00:52:56,919
I think I've broken something.

630
00:52:58,019 --> 00:53:00,319
Trust a Brandybuck and a Took!

631
00:53:00,319 --> 00:53:04,019
What? That was just a detour.
A short cut.

632
00:53:04,419 --> 00:53:06,619
- Short cut to what?
- Mushrooms!

633
00:53:15,419 --> 00:53:16,819
That's mine.

634
00:53:19,619 --> 00:53:21,219
That's nice, Merry.

635
00:53:21,819 --> 00:53:23,819
Here's a nice one, Sam.

636
00:53:23,819 --> 00:53:26,419
I think we should get off the road.

637
00:53:35,819 --> 00:53:37,120
Get off the road!

638
00:53:37,120 --> 00:53:38,720
Quick!

639
00:53:51,520 --> 00:53:52,920
Be quiet!

640
00:54:59,321 --> 00:55:01,421
What was that?

641
00:55:34,221 --> 00:55:35,621
Anything?

642
00:55:36,421 --> 00:55:37,821
Nothing.

643
00:55:38,621 --> 00:55:40,821
What is going on?

644
00:55:41,422 --> 00:55:45,022
That Black Rider was looking for something.
Or someone.

645
00:55:46,522 --> 00:55:47,922
Frodo?

646
00:55:48,722 --> 00:55:49,722
Get down!

647
00:56:06,622 --> 00:56:08,822
I have to leave the Shire.

648
00:56:09,922 --> 00:56:12,222
Sam and I must get to Bree.

649
00:56:12,222 --> 00:56:13,822
Right.

650
00:56:15,222 --> 00:56:17,422
Bucklebury Ferry. Follow me.

651
00:56:25,822 --> 00:56:27,022
Run!

652
00:56:28,322 --> 00:56:30,222
This way! Follow me!

653
00:56:34,022 --> 00:56:34,922
Run!

654
00:56:48,223 --> 00:56:49,923
Get the rope, Sam!

655
00:56:52,623 --> 00:56:54,123
Frodo!

656
00:56:54,923 --> 00:56:56,223
Run, Frodo!

657
00:56:56,723 --> 00:56:57,723
Go!
- Hurry!

658
00:56:57,723 --> 00:57:00,423
Frodo, come on!

659
00:57:01,523 --> 00:57:03,523
- Come on! Faster!
- Jump!

660
00:57:18,523 --> 00:57:22,523
- How far to the nearest crossing?
- The Brandywine Bridge. 20 miles.

661
00:57:37,323 --> 00:57:38,823
Come on.

662
00:57:50,024 --> 00:57:53,324
- What do you want?
- We're heading for the Prancing Pony.

663
00:57:56,924 --> 00:57:59,724
Hobbits. Four hobbits!

664
00:57:59,724 --> 00:58:03,724
What's more, out of the Shire by your talk.
What business brings you to Bree?

665
00:58:04,424 --> 00:58:07,424
We wish to stay at the inn.
Our business is our own.

666
00:58:08,624 --> 00:58:11,024
All right young sir, I meant no offense.

667
00:58:11,324 --> 00:58:13,724
It's my job to ask questions after nightfall.

668
00:58:14,124 --> 00:58:16,924
There's talk of strange folk abroad.

669
00:58:16,924 --> 00:58:19,224
Can't be too careful.

670
00:58:39,024 --> 00:58:42,324
Out of the way!
Watch where you're walking.

671
00:59:06,525 --> 00:59:08,025
Excuse me.

672
00:59:09,125 --> 00:59:11,825
Good evening, little masters.
What can I do for you?

673
00:59:12,125 --> 00:59:17,925
If you're looking for accommodation, we got
some nice cozy hobbit-sized rooms available.

674
00:59:18,425 --> 00:59:22,925
Always proud to cater to little folk, Mister...?

675
00:59:24,125 --> 00:59:26,125
Underhill. My name's Underhill.

676
00:59:27,525 --> 00:59:29,925
- Underhill, yeah.
- We're friends of Gandalf the Grey.

677
00:59:30,225 --> 00:59:33,225
- Can you tell him we've arrived?
- Gandalf?

678
00:59:33,725 --> 00:59:35,425
Gandalf.

679
00:59:36,325 --> 00:59:37,925
Oh, yes...

680
00:59:38,225 --> 00:59:40,225
...I remember. Elderly chap.

681
00:59:40,625 --> 00:59:43,525
Big grey beard, pointy hat.

682
00:59:43,925 --> 00:59:45,725
Not seen him for six months.

683
00:59:52,626 --> 00:59:53,926
What do we do now?

684
01:00:01,126 --> 01:00:02,326
Sam...

685
01:00:02,326 --> 01:00:04,326
...he'll be here. He'll come.

686
01:00:07,226 --> 01:00:09,226
Get out of my way!

687
01:00:11,726 --> 01:00:13,326
What's that?

688
01:00:13,326 --> 01:00:15,926
This, my friend, is a pint.

689
01:00:16,326 --> 01:00:17,826
It comes in pints?

690
01:00:18,226 --> 01:00:21,726
- I'm getting one.
- You got a whole half already!

691
01:00:28,226 --> 01:00:31,926
That fellow's done nothing but
stare at you since we arrived.

692
01:00:35,726 --> 01:00:37,126
Excuse me.

693
01:00:39,026 --> 01:00:41,826
That man in the corner. Who is he?

694
01:00:43,226 --> 01:00:47,426
He's one of them Rangers. They're dangerous
folk they are, wandering the wilds.

695
01:00:47,726 --> 01:00:52,126
What his right name is, I've never heard,
but 'round here he's known as Strider.

696
01:00:54,627 --> 01:00:55,827
Strider.

697
01:01:08,927 --> 01:01:12,027
<i>Baggins...</i>

698
01:01:15,227 --> 01:01:18,127
<i>Baggins...</i>

699
01:01:22,527 --> 01:01:24,827
<i>Baggins...</i>

700
01:01:26,127 --> 01:01:28,527
<i>Baggins...</i>

701
01:01:29,227 --> 01:01:32,127
<i>Baggins...
Baggins? Sure, I know a Baggins.</i>

702
01:01:32,827 --> 01:01:35,427
He's over there. Frodo Baggins.

703
01:01:35,427 --> 01:01:38,727
He's my second cousin,
once removed on his mother's side...

704
01:01:38,727 --> 01:01:41,027
...and my third cousin, twice removed....

705
01:01:45,627 --> 01:01:47,327
- Pippin!
- Steady on, Frodo.

706
01:02:16,928 --> 01:02:19,328
<i>You cannot hide.</i>

707
01:02:22,328 --> 01:02:25,328
<i>I see you.</i>

708
01:02:27,228 --> 01:02:29,828
<i>There is no life...</i>

709
01:02:29,828 --> 01:02:32,128
<i>...in the void.</i>

710
01:02:32,428 --> 01:02:33,828
<i>Only...</i>

711
01:02:34,828 --> 01:02:36,328
<i>...death.</i>

712
01:02:42,328 --> 01:02:47,028
You draw far too much attention
to yourself, "Mr. Underhill."

713
01:02:51,928 --> 01:02:52,828
What do you want?

714
01:02:53,128 --> 01:02:55,128
A little more caution from you.
That is no trinket you carry.

715
01:02:55,628 --> 01:02:58,529
- I carry nothing.
- Indeed.

716
01:02:58,929 --> 01:03:01,329
I can avoid being seen if I wish...

717
01:03:01,629 --> 01:03:05,129
...but to disappear entirely, that is a rare gift.

718
01:03:05,829 --> 01:03:08,329
- Who are you?
- Are you frightened?

719
01:03:09,729 --> 01:03:10,629
Yes.

720
01:03:10,629 --> 01:03:14,629
Not nearly frightened enough.
I know what hunts you.

721
01:03:18,729 --> 01:03:21,129
Let him go!
Or I'll have you, Longshanks.

722
01:03:23,029 --> 01:03:26,929
You have a stout heart, little hobbit.
But that will not save you.

723
01:03:27,329 --> 01:03:30,129
You can no longer wait for the wizard, Frodo.

724
01:03:30,429 --> 01:03:31,429
They're coming.

725
01:04:55,130 --> 01:04:56,530
What are they?

726
01:04:58,730 --> 01:05:00,830
They were once men.

727
01:05:01,130 --> 01:05:03,231
Great kings of men.

728
01:05:03,831 --> 01:05:06,831
Then Sauron the Deceiver gave to them
nine rings of power.

729
01:05:07,631 --> 01:05:10,631
Blinded by their greed,
they took them without question.

730
01:05:10,931 --> 01:05:14,131
One by one, falling into darkness.

731
01:05:14,431 --> 01:05:16,831
Now they are slaves to his will.

732
01:05:19,331 --> 01:05:20,931
They are the Nazgûl.

733
01:05:20,931 --> 01:05:23,731
Ringwraiths. Neither living nor dead.

734
01:05:24,731 --> 01:05:26,131
At all times they feel...

735
01:05:26,131 --> 01:05:28,131
... the presence of the ring...

736
01:05:28,431 --> 01:05:32,731
...drawn to the power of the One.
They will never stop hunting you.

737
01:05:42,931 --> 01:05:45,731
- Where are you taking us?
- Into the wild.

738
01:05:54,131 --> 01:05:57,931
How can we know this Strider
is a friend of Gandalf?

739
01:05:58,331 --> 01:06:01,131
I think a servant of the enemy would look fairer...

740
01:06:01,531 --> 01:06:05,332
...and feel fouler.
- He's foul enough.

741
01:06:06,032 --> 01:06:08,832
We have no choice but to trust him.

742
01:06:09,132 --> 01:06:12,332
- But where is he leading us?
- To Rivendell, Master Gamgee.

743
01:06:14,832 --> 01:06:18,032
- To the house of Elrond.
- Did you hear that? Rivendell.

744
01:06:18,732 --> 01:06:21,432
We're going to see the elves.

745
01:06:43,132 --> 01:06:47,232
- Gentlemen, we do not stop till nightfall.
- What about breakfast?

746
01:06:47,532 --> 01:06:50,232
- You've already had it.
- We've had one, yes.

747
01:06:50,232 --> 01:06:52,632
What about second breakfast?

748
01:06:56,032 --> 01:06:59,032
Don't think he knows about second breakfast, Pip.

749
01:06:59,532 --> 01:07:04,532
What about elevenses? Luncheon?
Afternoon tea? Dinner? Supper?

750
01:07:04,932 --> 01:07:08,933
- He knows about them, doesn't he?
- I wouldn't count on it.

751
01:07:14,533 --> 01:07:16,133
Pippin!

752
01:07:32,633 --> 01:07:35,933
What do they eat when they can't get Hobbit?

753
01:07:51,433 --> 01:07:54,733
<i>"Tinúviel elvanui
(Tinúviel the elven-fair)</i>

754
01:07:56,633 --> 01:08:02,933
<i>Elleth alfirin ethelhael
(Immortal maiden elven-wise)</i>

755
01:08:04,333 --> 01:08:10,234
<i>O hon ring finnil fuinui
(About him cast her night-dark hair)</i>

756
01:08:10,734 --> 01:08:14,734
<i>A renc gelebrin thiliol."
(And arms like silver glimmering.")</i>

757
01:08:15,034 --> 01:08:17,134
Who is she?

758
01:08:17,934 --> 01:08:20,334
This woman you sing of.

759
01:08:23,834 --> 01:08:26,234
'Tis the Lay of Lúthien.

760
01:08:26,234 --> 01:08:31,434
The elf-maiden who gave her
love to Beren, a mortal.

761
01:08:33,434 --> 01:08:35,534
What happened to her?

762
01:08:37,834 --> 01:08:40,234
She died.

763
01:08:44,234 --> 01:08:46,534
Get some sleep, Frodo.

764
01:08:57,034 --> 01:09:00,934
The power of Isengard is at your command...

765
01:09:01,234 --> 01:09:05,434
... Sauron, Lord of the Earth.

766
01:09:09,034 --> 01:09:14,635
Build me an army worthy of Mordor.

767
01:09:20,335 --> 01:09:24,635
What orders from Mordor, my lord?
What does the Eye command?

768
01:09:25,335 --> 01:09:27,135
We have work to do.

769
01:10:10,035 --> 01:10:14,436
The trees are strong, my lord.
Their roots go deep.

770
01:10:15,036 --> 01:10:16,836
Rip them all down.

771
01:10:44,336 --> 01:10:47,036
This was the great watchtower of Amon Sûl.

772
01:10:48,836 --> 01:10:51,336
We shall rest here tonight.

773
01:11:03,136 --> 01:11:06,436
These are for you.
Keep them close.

774
01:11:06,836 --> 01:11:09,236
I'm going to have a look around.

775
01:11:11,736 --> 01:11:13,536
Stay here.

776
01:11:16,136 --> 01:11:18,337
My tomato's burst.

777
01:11:18,337 --> 01:11:20,437
Could I have some bacon?

778
01:11:20,437 --> 01:11:22,537
Want a tomato, Sam?

779
01:11:22,937 --> 01:11:26,537
- What are you doing?!
- Tomatoes, sausages, nice crispy bacon.

780
01:11:26,837 --> 01:11:29,437
- We saved some for you, Mr. Frodo.
- Put it out, you fools!

781
01:11:29,737 --> 01:11:33,537
- Put it out!
- That's nice! Ash on my tomatoes!

782
01:11:42,137 --> 01:11:43,837
Go!

783
01:12:37,438 --> 01:12:38,838
Back, you devils!

784
01:12:49,029 --> 01:12:50,998
[Black Speech] <i>Gûm-ishi...</i>
[English] In the void...

785
01:12:52,998 --> 01:12:53,998
[Black Speech] <i>...ashi...</i>
[English] ...only...

786
01:13:13,498 --> 01:13:15,498
[Black Speech] <i>...gurum!</i>
[English] ...death!

787
01:14:02,339 --> 01:14:03,539
Frodo!

788
01:14:08,239 --> 01:14:09,439
Oh, Sam.

789
01:14:46,540 --> 01:14:47,540
Strider!

790
01:14:50,240 --> 01:14:55,540
- Help him, Strider.
- He's been stabbed by a Morgul blade.

791
01:14:57,240 --> 01:15:01,940
This is beyond my skill to heal.
He needs elvish medicine.

792
01:15:06,740 --> 01:15:07,740
Hurry!

793
01:15:08,040 --> 01:15:11,840
We're six days from Rivendell!
He'll never make it!

794
01:15:12,140 --> 01:15:13,940
Hold on, Frodo.

795
01:15:14,540 --> 01:15:16,540
Gandalf!

796
01:16:20,001 --> 01:16:22,001
... Gwaihir, go!

797
01:17:54,743 --> 01:17:57,643
Look, Frodo. It's Mr. Bilbo's trolls.

798
01:17:59,943 --> 01:18:02,643
Mr. Frodo? He's going cold.

799
01:18:05,643 --> 01:18:07,343
Is he going to die?

800
01:18:07,643 --> 01:18:12,343
He's passing into the shadow world.
He'll soon become a wraith like them.

801
01:18:17,643 --> 01:18:21,343
- They're close.
- Sam, do you know the Athelas plant?

802
01:18:21,743 --> 01:18:23,143
- Athelas?
- Kingsfoil.

803
01:18:23,143 --> 01:18:24,343
Kingsfoil, aye, it's a weed.

804
01:18:24,643 --> 01:18:27,643
It may help to slow the poisoning.
Hurry!

805
01:18:42,144 --> 01:18:46,144
What's this, a ranger caught off his guard?

806
01:19:11,244 --> 01:19:12,544
Frodo.

807
01:19:13,694 --> 01:19:18,094
[Sindarin] <i>Im Arwen, Telin le thaed.</i>
[English] I Arwen, I come to help you.

808
01:19:19,344 --> 01:19:23,494
[Sindarin] <i>Lasto beth nîn, tolo dan nan galad.</i>
[English] Listen to my word, come back to the light.

809
01:19:29,044 --> 01:19:30,844
Who is she?

810
01:19:31,544 --> 01:19:33,244
Frodo.

811
01:19:33,544 --> 01:19:36,945
- She's an elf.
- He's fading.

812
01:19:39,545 --> 01:19:41,545
He's not going to last.

813
01:19:41,845 --> 01:19:44,345
We must get him to my father.

814
01:19:45,145 --> 01:19:47,945
- I've been looking for you for two days.
- Where are you taking him?

815
01:19:48,245 --> 01:19:54,145
There are five wraiths behind you.
Where the other four are, I do not know.

816
01:19:55,045 --> 01:19:57,765
[Sindarin] <i>Dartho guin Beriain. Rych le ad tolthathon.</i>
[English] Stay with the Hobbits. I will send horses for you.

817
01:19:57,765 --> 01:20:00,245
[Sindarin] <i>Hon mabathon! Rochon ellint im.</i>
[English] I will take him! I am the swifter rider.

818
01:20:00,245 --> 01:20:01,735
[Sindarin] <i>Andelu i ven.</i>
[English] The road is too dangerous.

819
01:20:02,145 --> 01:20:03,345
What are they saying?

820
01:20:03,135 --> 01:20:05,675
[Sindarin] <i>Frodo fîr. Ae athradon i hîr ...</i>
[English] Frodo is dying. If I cross the river ...

821
01:20:05,675 --> 01:20:08,895
[Sindarin] <i>... tûr gwaith nîn beriatha hon.</i>
[English] ... the power of my people will protect him.

822
01:20:09,545 --> 01:20:11,045
I do not fear them.

823
01:20:14,765 --> 01:20:15,725
[Sindarin] <i>Be iest lîn.</i>
[English] As you wish.

824
01:20:21,045 --> 01:20:22,445
Arwen...

825
01:20:22,445 --> 01:20:25,645
...ride hard. Don't Look back.

826
01:20:24,805 --> 01:20:26,995
[Sindarin] <i>Noro lim Asfaloth, noro lim!</i>
[English] Ride fast Asfaloth, ride fast!

827
01:20:30,845 --> 01:20:35,045
What are you doing?!
Those wraiths are still out there!

828
01:21:45,207 --> 01:21:47,007
[Sindarin] <i>Noro lim Asfaloth!</i>
[English] Ride fast Asfaloth!

829
01:22:29,747 --> 01:22:33,147
Give up the halfling, She-elf.

830
01:22:33,547 --> 01:22:35,947
If you want him, come and claim him.

831
01:22:48,008 --> 01:22:50,528
[Sindarin] <i>Nîn o Chithaeglir, lasto beth daer!</i>
[English] Waters of the Misty Mountains, listen to the great word!

832
01:22:50,538 --> 01:22:53,648
[Sindarin] <i>Rimmo nîn Bruinen dan in Ulaer!</i>
[English] Flow waters of Loudwater against the Ringwraiths!

833
01:22:53,648 --> 01:22:56,798
[Sindarin] <i>Nîn o Chithaeglir, lasto beth daer!</i>
[English] Waters of the Misty Mountains, listen to the great word!

834
01:22:56,798 --> 01:23:00,178
[Sindarin] <i>Rimmo nîn Bruinen dan in Ulaer!</i>
[English] Flow waters of Loudwater against the Ringwraiths!

835
01:23:29,948 --> 01:23:32,348
No. No!

836
01:23:35,648 --> 01:23:37,848
Frodo, no.

837
01:23:38,148 --> 01:23:40,348
Frodo, don't give in.

838
01:23:40,648 --> 01:23:42,548
Not now.

839
01:23:53,649 --> 01:23:56,049
What grace is given me...

840
01:23:56,749 --> 01:23:58,549
...let it pass to him.

841
01:23:58,849 --> 01:24:00,949
Let him be spared.

842
01:24:01,649 --> 01:24:03,549
Save him.

843
01:24:05,509 --> 01:24:09,599
[Sindarin] <i>Lasto beth nîn. Tolo dan nan galad.</i>
[English] Hear my voice. Come back to the light.

844
01:24:16,049 --> 01:24:21,049
- Where am I?
- You are in the house of Elrond.

845
01:24:21,649 --> 01:24:27,849
And it is 10 o'clock in the morning
on October 24th, if you want to know.

846
01:24:30,149 --> 01:24:33,749
- Gandalf!
- Yes, I'm here.

847
01:24:35,649 --> 01:24:38,549
And you're lucky to be here too.

848
01:24:39,249 --> 01:24:43,149
A few more hours and you would
have been beyond our aid.

849
01:24:43,549 --> 01:24:47,449
But you have some strength in you,
my dear Hobbit.

850
01:24:55,250 --> 01:24:57,650
What happened, Gandalf?

851
01:24:58,650 --> 01:25:03,950
- Why didn't you meet us?
- I am sorry, Frodo.

852
01:25:08,750 --> 01:25:10,450
I was delayed.

853
01:25:11,550 --> 01:25:15,550
A friendship with Saruman
is not lightly thrown aside.

854
01:25:19,850 --> 01:25:24,350
One ill turn deserves another. It is over.

855
01:25:24,850 --> 01:25:27,450
Embrace the power of the ring...

856
01:25:28,150 --> 01:25:30,550
...or embrace your own destruction!

857
01:25:32,950 --> 01:25:36,650
There is only one lord of the ring.

858
01:25:37,150 --> 01:25:40,950
Only one who can bend it to his will.

859
01:25:41,950 --> 01:25:45,750
And he does not share power.

860
01:26:00,151 --> 01:26:03,351
So you have chosen...death.

861
01:26:13,651 --> 01:26:17,251
Gandalf? What is it?

862
01:26:18,451 --> 01:26:20,151
Nothing, Frodo.

863
01:26:20,851 --> 01:26:22,751
Frodo!

864
01:26:24,151 --> 01:26:26,351
- Sam.
- Bless you, you're awake!

865
01:26:26,751 --> 01:26:29,351
Sam has hardly left your side.

866
01:26:29,751 --> 01:26:31,751
We were that worried about you.
Weren't we, Mr. Gandalf?

867
01:26:32,351 --> 01:26:37,251
By the skills of Lord Elrond,
you're beginning to mend.

868
01:26:38,851 --> 01:26:42,351
Welcome to Rivendell, Frodo Baggins.

869
01:27:30,552 --> 01:27:33,652
- Bilbo!
- Hello, Frodo, my lad.

870
01:27:34,052 --> 01:27:35,752
Bilbo.

871
01:27:40,652 --> 01:27:42,652
There and back again

872
01:27:42,652 --> 01:27:45,352
A hobbit's Tale, by Bilbo Baggins.''

873
01:27:48,552 --> 01:27:51,952
- This is wonderful.
- I meant to go back...

874
01:27:52,352 --> 01:27:56,053
...wonder at the powers of Mirkwood...

875
01:27:56,653 --> 01:27:58,853
...visit Lake-town...

876
01:27:59,153 --> 01:28:02,453
...see the Lonely Mountain again.

877
01:28:03,153 --> 01:28:07,753
But age, it seems, has finally caught up with me.

878
01:28:20,153 --> 01:28:21,853
I miss the Shire.

879
01:28:22,353 --> 01:28:27,253
I spent all my childhood pretending
I was off somewhere else.

880
01:28:27,753 --> 01:28:31,153
Off with you, on one of your adventures.

881
01:28:34,153 --> 01:28:37,653
But my own adventure turned out
to be quite different.

882
01:28:43,153 --> 01:28:46,153
I'm not like you, Bilbo.

883
01:28:47,553 --> 01:28:49,653
My dear boy.

884
01:28:53,953 --> 01:28:57,654
- Now, what have I forgotten?
- Packed already?

885
01:28:58,554 --> 01:29:00,254
No harm in being prepared.

886
01:29:00,554 --> 01:29:03,054
- I thought you wanted to see the elves.
- I do.

887
01:29:03,354 --> 01:29:06,054
- More than anything.
- I did.

888
01:29:06,454 --> 01:29:08,354
It's just....

889
01:29:09,154 --> 01:29:11,654
We did what Gandalf wanted, didn't we?

890
01:29:11,954 --> 01:29:15,454
We got the ring this far, to Rivendell.
And I thought...

891
01:29:15,954 --> 01:29:19,054
...seeing as how you're on the mend,
we'd be off soon.

892
01:29:19,354 --> 01:29:20,954
Off home.

893
01:29:25,154 --> 01:29:27,054
You are right, Sam.

894
01:29:29,354 --> 01:29:32,054
We did what we set out to do.

895
01:29:32,654 --> 01:29:35,154
The ring will be safe in Rivendell.

896
01:29:39,354 --> 01:29:41,654
I am ready to go home.

897
01:29:42,454 --> 01:29:44,354
His strength returns.

898
01:29:44,654 --> 01:29:50,154
That wound will never fully heal.
He will carry it the rest of his life.

899
01:29:51,054 --> 01:29:53,454
And yet to have come so far still bearing the ring...

900
01:29:53,454 --> 01:29:57,254
...the Hobbit has shown extraordinary
resilience to its evil.

901
01:29:57,654 --> 01:30:00,955
It is a burden he should never have had to bear.

902
01:30:01,255 --> 01:30:06,455
- We can ask no more of Frodo.
- Gandalf, the enemy is moving.

903
01:30:06,855 --> 01:30:11,355
Sauron's forces are massing in the East.
His eye is fixed on Rivendell.

904
01:30:11,755 --> 01:30:14,355
And Saruman, you tell me, has betrayed us.

905
01:30:14,755 --> 01:30:17,855
Our list of allies grows thin.

906
01:30:18,655 --> 01:30:21,355
His treachery runs deeper than you know.

907
01:30:21,655 --> 01:30:25,155
By foul craft, Saruman
has crossed orcs with goblin-men.

908
01:30:25,555 --> 01:30:27,855
He's breeding an army in the caverns of Isengard.

909
01:30:28,255 --> 01:30:32,655
An army that can move in sunlight
and cover great distance at speed.

910
01:30:33,055 --> 01:30:35,355
Saruman is coming for the ring.

911
01:30:35,855 --> 01:30:39,755
This evil cannot be concealed
by the power of the elves.

912
01:30:40,155 --> 01:30:44,355
We do not have the strength to
fight both Mordor and Isengard!

913
01:30:48,355 --> 01:30:49,355
Gandalf...

914
01:30:50,755 --> 01:30:53,155
...the ring cannot stay here.

915
01:31:12,856 --> 01:31:15,956
This peril belongs to all Middle-earth.

916
01:31:16,256 --> 01:31:18,956
They must decide now how to end it.

917
01:31:20,056 --> 01:31:23,456
The time of the elves is over.
My people are leaving these shores.

918
01:31:24,256 --> 01:31:27,756
Who will you look to when we've gone?
The dwarves?

919
01:31:28,156 --> 01:31:33,056
They hide in mountains seeking riches.
They care not for the troubles of others.

920
01:31:34,756 --> 01:31:37,556
It is in men that we must place our hope.

921
01:31:38,056 --> 01:31:39,656
Men?

922
01:31:40,656 --> 01:31:43,656
Men are weak. The race of men is failing.

923
01:31:44,056 --> 01:31:48,256
The blood of Numenor is all but spent,
its pride and dignity forgotten.

924
01:31:48,756 --> 01:31:52,156
It is because of men the ring survives.

925
01:31:52,556 --> 01:31:54,056
I was there, Gandalf.

926
01:31:54,856 --> 01:31:57,556
I was there 3000 years ago...

927
01:32:04,457 --> 01:32:06,757
... when Isildur took the ring.

928
01:32:07,057 --> 01:32:10,757
I was there the day the strength of men failed.

929
01:32:13,457 --> 01:32:15,957
Isildur, hurry! Follow me.

930
01:32:17,657 --> 01:32:21,157
I led Isildur into the heart of Mount Doom...

931
01:32:21,557 --> 01:32:24,957
...where the ring was forged,
the one place it could be destroyed.

932
01:32:24,957 --> 01:32:27,657
Cast it into the fire!

933
01:32:32,957 --> 01:32:36,557
- Destroy it!
- No.

934
01:32:38,057 --> 01:32:40,157
Isildur!

935
01:32:40,657 --> 01:32:45,257
It should have ended that day,
but evil was allowed to endure.

936
01:32:49,557 --> 01:32:53,657
Isildur kept the ring.
The line of kings is broken.

937
01:32:54,657 --> 01:32:58,257
There's no strength left in the world of men.

938
01:32:58,657 --> 01:33:03,257
- They're scattered, divided, leaderless.
- There is one who could unite them.

939
01:33:03,657 --> 01:33:06,858
One who could reclaim the throne of Gondor.

940
01:33:08,758 --> 01:33:12,358
He turned from that path a long time ago.

941
01:33:12,658 --> 01:33:14,758
He has chosen exile.

942
01:33:45,858 --> 01:33:47,758
You are no elf.

943
01:33:48,058 --> 01:33:50,058
Men of the South are welcome here.

944
01:33:50,758 --> 01:33:54,158
- Who are you?
- I am a friend to Gandalf the Grey.

945
01:33:55,758 --> 01:33:58,458
Then we are here on common purpose...

946
01:33:58,858 --> 01:34:00,258
...friend.

947
01:34:15,659 --> 01:34:18,459
The shards of Narsil.

948
01:34:22,059 --> 01:34:26,259
The blade that cut the ring from Sauron's hand.

949
01:34:29,359 --> 01:34:31,559
It's still sharp.

950
01:34:40,559 --> 01:34:43,459
But no more than a broken heirloom.

951
01:35:10,459 --> 01:35:13,460
Why do you fear the past?

952
01:35:14,360 --> 01:35:19,460
You are Isildur's heir, not Isildur himseIf.

953
01:35:19,960 --> 01:35:23,260
You are not bound to his fate.

954
01:35:23,860 --> 01:35:27,660
The same blood flows in my veins.

955
01:35:30,860 --> 01:35:33,360
The same weakness.

956
01:35:36,160 --> 01:35:38,860
Your time will come.

957
01:35:39,160 --> 01:35:43,360
You will face the same evil.
And you will defeat it.

958
01:35:46,220 --> 01:35:48,930
[Sindarin] <i>A si i-Dhúath ú-orthor, Aragorn.</i>
[English] The shadow does not hold sway yet, Aragorn.

959
01:35:49,920 --> 01:35:53,510
[Sindarin] <i>Ú or le a ú or nin.</i>
[English] Not over you, not over me.

960
01:36:04,670 --> 01:36:07,910
[Sindarin] <i>Renich i lú i erui govannem?</i>
[English] Do you remember when we first met?

961
01:36:11,400 --> 01:36:15,431
[Sindarin] <i>Nauthannen i ned ôl reniannen.</i>
[English] I thought I had strayed into a dream.

962
01:36:16,331 --> 01:36:19,011
[Sindarin] <i>Gwenwin in enninath.</i>
[English] Long years have passed.

963
01:36:20,051 --> 01:36:23,711
[Sindarin] <i>Ú-'arnech in naeth i si celich.</i>
[English] You did not wear the troubles you carry now.

964
01:36:25,551 --> 01:36:27,851
[Sindarin] <i>Renich i beth i pennen?</i>
[English] Do you remember what I told you?

965
01:36:34,061 --> 01:36:36,661
You said you'd bind yourself to me...

966
01:36:38,861 --> 01:36:43,561
...forsaking the immortal life of your people.

967
01:36:44,861 --> 01:36:46,761
And to that I hold.

968
01:36:46,761 --> 01:36:50,461
I would rather share one lifetime with you...

969
01:36:50,961 --> 01:36:54,561
...than face all the ages of this world alone.

970
01:37:03,461 --> 01:37:06,761
I choose a mortal life.

971
01:37:08,261 --> 01:37:12,361
- You cannot give me this.
- It is mine to give to whom I will...

972
01:37:15,761 --> 01:37:18,162
...like my heart.

973
01:37:34,062 --> 01:37:37,662
Strangers from distant lands, friends of old...

974
01:37:38,062 --> 01:37:41,762
...you've been summoned here
to answer the threat of Mordor.

975
01:37:42,562 --> 01:37:47,262
Middle-earth stands upon the brink of destruction.
None can escape it.

976
01:37:47,662 --> 01:37:51,062
You will unite, or you will fall.

977
01:37:51,462 --> 01:37:55,562
Each race is bound to this fate, this one doom.

978
01:37:57,562 --> 01:38:00,862
Bring forth the ring, Frodo.

979
01:38:15,162 --> 01:38:16,762
So it is true.

980
01:38:26,563 --> 01:38:28,063
<i>The ring of power...</i>

981
01:38:30,163 --> 01:38:31,663
<i>The doom of men...</i>

982
01:38:34,263 --> 01:38:36,263
In a dream...

983
01:38:38,063 --> 01:38:41,163
...I saw the eastern sky grow dark...

984
01:38:41,463 --> 01:38:43,163
...but in the West a pale light lingered.

985
01:38:43,963 --> 01:38:45,763
A voice was crying:

986
01:38:46,063 --> 01:38:48,863
"Your doom is near at hand.

987
01:38:50,063 --> 01:38:52,663
Isildur's bane is found."

988
01:38:54,793 --> 01:38:56,193
(The Ring)
[Black Speech] <i>Sherkuk-ishi</i>
[English] In your blood

989
01:38:56,663 --> 01:38:58,463
Isildur s bane.

990
01:38:59,063 --> 01:38:59,363
Boromir!

991
01:38:59,324 --> 01:39:03,093
(Gandalf)
[Black Speech] <i>Ash nazg durbatulûk...</i>
[English] One ring to rule them all...

992
01:39:00,673 --> 01:39:03,373
{\an8} (The Ring)
{\an8} [Black Speech] <i>Shre nazg golugranu kilmi-nudu...</i>
{\an8} [English] Three Rings for the Elven-kings under the sky...

993
01:39:03,093 --> 01:39:06,803
(Gandalf)
[Black Speech] <i>...Ash nazg gimbatul...</i>
[English] ...One ring to find them...

994
01:39:06,627 --> 01:39:10,889
{\an8} (The Ring)
{\an8} [Black Speech] <i>Ombi kuzd-durbagu... shirku</i>
{\an8} [English] Seven for the Dwarf-lords... blood

995
01:39:07,013 --> 01:39:10,183
(Gandalf)
[Black Speech] <i>...Ash nazg thrakatulûk...</i>
[English] ...One ring to bring them all...

996
01:39:11,207 --> 01:39:14,669
{\an8} (The Ring)
{\an8} [Black Speech] <i>Ash Burz-Durbagu burzum-ishi...</i>
{\an8} [English] One for the Dark lord on his dark throne...

997
01:39:13,093 --> 01:39:17,413
(Gandalf)
[Black Speech] <i>...Agh burzum-ishi krimpatul.</i>
[English] ...and in the darkness bind them.

998
01:39:23,564 --> 01:39:27,264
Never before has any voice uttered the
words of that tongue here in Imladris.

999
01:39:27,664 --> 01:39:31,164
I do not ask your pardon, Master Elrond...

1000
01:39:31,464 --> 01:39:33,464
...for the black speech of Mordor...

1001
01:39:33,864 --> 01:39:35,164
...may yet be heard...

1002
01:39:35,464 --> 01:39:38,264
...in every corner of the West!

1003
01:39:38,564 --> 01:39:41,164
The ring is altogether evil.

1004
01:39:41,664 --> 01:39:43,064
It is a gift.

1005
01:39:43,864 --> 01:39:45,764
A gift to the foes of Mordor.

1006
01:39:46,464 --> 01:39:48,464
Why not use this ring?

1007
01:39:48,764 --> 01:39:51,464
Long has my father, the Steward of Gondor...

1008
01:39:51,764 --> 01:39:55,864
...kept the forces of Mordor at bay.
By the blood of our people...

1009
01:39:56,364 --> 01:39:58,464
...are your lands kept safe.

1010
01:40:00,264 --> 01:40:04,464
Give Gondor the weapon of the enemy.
Let us use it against him.

1011
01:40:04,864 --> 01:40:08,464
You cannot wield it. None of us can.

1012
01:40:09,264 --> 01:40:13,164
The one ring answers to Sauron alone.
It has no other master.

1013
01:40:13,564 --> 01:40:16,964
And what would a ranger know of this matter?

1014
01:40:17,264 --> 01:40:19,164
This is no mere ranger.

1015
01:40:20,264 --> 01:40:23,765
He is Aragorn, son of Arathorn.

1016
01:40:24,465 --> 01:40:27,265
You owe him your allegiance.

1017
01:40:31,465 --> 01:40:33,365
Aragorn.

1018
01:40:35,165 --> 01:40:37,965
This is Isildur s heir?

1019
01:40:40,365 --> 01:40:43,065
And heir to the throne of Gondor.

1020
01:40:44,545 --> 01:40:46,445
[Sindarin] <i>Havo dad, Legolas.</i>
[English] Sit down, Legolas.

1021
01:40:49,965 --> 01:40:52,765
Gondor has no king.

1022
01:40:54,765 --> 01:40:56,365
Gondor needs no king.

1023
01:41:03,065 --> 01:41:06,565
Aragorn is right. We cannot use it.

1024
01:41:07,765 --> 01:41:11,065
You have only one choice.

1025
01:41:11,365 --> 01:41:13,665
The ring must be destroyed.

1026
01:41:18,965 --> 01:41:21,465
What are we waiting for?

1027
01:41:26,716 --> 01:41:31,828
[Black Speech] <i>Daghburz-ishi makha, ghurarmu shirku.</i>
[English] In the land of Mordor, a sacrifice of blood.

1028
01:41:33,666 --> 01:41:36,566
The ring cannot be destroyed, Gimli, son of Gloin...

1029
01:41:36,966 --> 01:41:41,066
...by any craft that we here possess.

1030
01:41:41,766 --> 01:41:45,666
The ring was made in the fires of Mount Doom.

1031
01:41:46,166 --> 01:41:49,766
Only there can it be unmade.

1032
01:41:51,066 --> 01:41:53,466
It must be taken deep into Mordor...

1033
01:41:53,766 --> 01:41:58,066
...and cast back into the fiery
chasm from whence it came.

1034
01:41:57,471 --> 01:42:00,506
[Black Speech] <i>Makha gulshu darulu.</i>
[English] Where the Shadows lie.

1035
01:42:00,566 --> 01:42:02,666
One of you...

1036
01:42:03,266 --> 01:42:05,366
...must do this.

1037
01:42:08,366 --> 01:42:11,966
One does not simply walk into Mordor.

1038
01:42:12,966 --> 01:42:16,466
Its black gates are guarded by more than just orcs.

1039
01:42:17,366 --> 01:42:21,366
There is evil there that does not sleep.

1040
01:42:21,766 --> 01:42:25,866
The great eye is ever-watchful.

1041
01:42:26,766 --> 01:42:28,667
It is a barren wasteland...

1042
01:42:29,067 --> 01:42:32,367
...riddled with fire, and ash and dust.

1043
01:42:32,767 --> 01:42:36,567
The very air you breathe is a poisonous fume.

1044
01:42:36,867 --> 01:42:40,967
Not with 10,000 men could you do this.
It is folly.

1045
01:42:41,367 --> 01:42:45,667
Have you heard nothing Lord Elrond has said?
The ring must be destroyed.

1046
01:42:46,067 --> 01:42:48,467
And I suppose you think you are the one to do it!

1047
01:42:48,767 --> 01:42:53,267
And if we fail, what then? What happens
when Sauron takes back what is his?

1048
01:42:53,667 --> 01:42:58,767
I will be dead before I see the
ring in the hands of an elf!

1049
01:43:00,967 --> 01:43:03,367
Never trust an elf!

1050
01:43:04,667 --> 01:43:10,267
Do you not understand? While you bicker
amongst yourselves, Sauron's power grows!

1051
01:43:10,767 --> 01:43:13,567
None can escape it!
You'll all be destroyed!

1052
01:43:14,117 --> 01:43:16,897
[Black Speech] <i>Ash nazg durbatulûk...</i>
[English] One ring to rule them all...

1053
01:43:16,897 --> 01:43:19,407
[Black Speech] <i>...Ash nazg gimbatul.</i>
[English] ...One ring to find them.

1054
01:43:19,417 --> 01:43:21,507
[Black Speech] <i>Ash nazg durbatulûk...</i>
[English] One ring to rule them all...

1055
01:43:21,517 --> 01:43:23,617
[Black Speech] <i>...Ash nazg gimbatul.</i>
[English] ...One ring to find them.

1056
01:43:23,617 --> 01:43:25,607
[Black Speech] <i>Ash nazg durbatulûk...</i>
[English] One ring to rule them all...

1057
01:43:25,617 --> 01:43:27,817
[Black Speech] <i>...Ash nazg gimbatul.</i>
[English] ...One ring to find them.

1058
01:43:27,817 --> 01:43:29,717
[Black Speech] <i>Ash nazg durbatulûk...</i>
[English] One ring to rule them all...

1059
01:43:32,368 --> 01:43:34,368
I will take it.

1060
01:43:36,668 --> 01:43:39,168
I will take it.

1061
01:43:44,968 --> 01:43:47,968
I will take the ring to Mordor.

1062
01:43:56,268 --> 01:43:57,368
Though...

1063
01:44:00,568 --> 01:44:02,368
...I do not know the way.

1064
01:44:04,368 --> 01:44:08,468
I will help you bear this burden, Frodo Baggins...

1065
01:44:08,868 --> 01:44:12,168
...as long as it is yours to bear.

1066
01:44:13,368 --> 01:44:16,368
If by my life or death I can protect you...

1067
01:44:17,168 --> 01:44:18,468
...I will.

1068
01:44:21,768 --> 01:44:23,968
You have my sword.

1069
01:44:25,868 --> 01:44:27,868
And you have my bow.

1070
01:44:28,568 --> 01:44:30,868
And my ax.

1071
01:44:38,069 --> 01:44:40,869
You carry the fates of us all, little one.

1072
01:44:43,069 --> 01:44:46,569
If this is indeed the will of the Council...

1073
01:44:47,269 --> 01:44:49,669
...then Gondor will see it done.

1074
01:44:52,269 --> 01:44:56,869
- Mr. Frodo's not going anywhere without me.
- No indeed it is hardly possible to separate you...

1075
01:44:57,269 --> 01:45:01,969
...even when he is summoned to a
secret council and you are not.

1076
01:45:02,669 --> 01:45:04,469
Oy. We're coming too!

1077
01:45:06,669 --> 01:45:09,369
You'll have to send us home
tied up in a sack to stop us.

1078
01:45:09,369 --> 01:45:12,769
Anyway, you need people
of intelligence on this sort of...

1079
01:45:13,269 --> 01:45:14,469
...mission.

1080
01:45:14,469 --> 01:45:16,019
Quest.

1081
01:45:16,519 --> 01:45:17,519
Thing.

1082
01:45:19,319 --> 01:45:22,019
Well, that rules you out, Pip.

1083
01:45:23,719 --> 01:45:25,519
Nine companions.

1084
01:45:27,319 --> 01:45:29,119
So be it.

1085
01:45:29,519 --> 01:45:32,519
You shall be: The Fellowship of the Ring.

1086
01:45:33,219 --> 01:45:35,019
Great!

1087
01:45:35,420 --> 01:45:37,520
Where are we going?

